    "This data was saved by a newer app version. Update Little Lift; the original file is preserved.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This data was saved by a newer app version. Update Little Lift; the original file is preserved."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Estos datos pertenecen a una versión más reciente. Actualiza Little Lift; se conserva el archivo original."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Observations are optional data with schema version 1. Omit observations for ordinary logging. Supported kinds: performance (user-confirmed load/reps versus targets), loggingInterval (Log-tap events/intervals, including exercise time; never actual rest or set duration), effort (one optional 1–10 rating after one specified exercise's final set). Use at most 12 requests and 100 total sets with observations. Give each request a unique stable 1–64 character id using letters, digits, hyphens or underscores; use each kind once per exercise. exerciseID must refer to the exercise's UUID id; retain IDs for unchanged requests. Only effort has afterSet, which must equal that exercise's sets. Actual rest, rep timing, technique, medical assessment, scripts and other kinds are unsupported; do not request them. No mandatory set-start taps or motion collection occur.\nFor comparisons across workouts, supply comparisonID and loadConvention together. comparisonID (same 1–64 character rules) identifies the exact equipment, variation, angle and grip; keep it stable only for that same variation. loadConvention is total, perDumbbell, machineStack, assistance or bodyweight. Bodyweight uses weight 0. Compare only matching comparisonID, unit and loadConvention; missing metadata means insufficient data, never a name-based match. An assistance setting is not lifted load. No automatic conversions or medical/causal conclusions. The user reviews all requests before accepting the plan.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Observations are optional data with schema version 1. Omit observations for ordinary logging. Supported kinds: performance (user-confirmed load/reps versus targets), loggingInterval (Log-tap events/intervals, including exercise time; never actual rest or set duration), effort (one optional 1–10 rating after one specified exercise's final set). Use at most 12 requests and 100 total sets with observations. Give each request a unique stable 1–64 character id using letters, digits, hyphens or underscores; use each kind once per exercise. exerciseID must refer to the exercise's UUID id; retain IDs for unchanged requests. Only effort has afterSet, which must equal that exercise's sets. Actual rest, rep timing, technique, medical assessment, scripts and other kinds are unsupported; do not request them. No mandatory set-start taps or motion collection occur.\nFor comparisons across workouts, supply comparisonID and loadConvention together. comparisonID (same 1–64 character rules) identifies the exact equipment, variation, angle and grip; keep it stable only for that same variation. loadConvention is total, perDumbbell, machineStack, assistance or bodyweight. Bodyweight uses weight 0. Compare only matching comparisonID, unit and loadConvention; missing metadata means insufficient data, never a name-based match. An assistance setting is not lifted load. No automatic conversions or medical/causal conclusions. The user reviews all requests before accepting the plan."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Las observaciones son datos opcionales con observationSchemaVersion: 1. Omítelas para un registro normal. Tipos admitidos: performance (carga y repeticiones confirmadas frente a objetivos), loggingInterval (eventos e intervalos entre toques en Registrar; incluyen ejecución y nunca miden descanso real ni duración de serie), effort (una valoración opcional de 1 a 10 tras la última serie de un ejercicio concreto). Máximo 12 solicitudes y 100 series si hay observaciones. Cada solicitud necesita un id único y estable de 1 a 64 caracteres: letras, números, guion o guion bajo. Usa cada tipo una vez por ejercicio. exerciseID debe coincidir con el UUID id del ejercicio; conserva los identificadores si no cambia la solicitud. Solo effort lleva afterSet, igual al número de series del ejercicio. No se admiten descanso real, tiempo de repetición, técnica, evaluación médica, scripts ni otros tipos. No se requieren toques de inicio de serie ni captura de movimiento.\nPara comparar sesiones, incluye comparisonID y loadConvention juntos. comparisonID (mismas reglas de 1 a 64 caracteres) identifica equipo, variante, ángulo y agarre exactos; mantenlo solo para esa misma variante. loadConvention admite total, perDumbbell, machineStack, assistance o bodyweight. bodyweight usa weight 0. Compara solo el mismo comparisonID, unit y loadConvention; sin metadatos hay datos insuficientes, nunca una equivalencia por nombre. Una asistencia no es carga levantada. No hagas conversiones automáticas ni conclusiones médicas o causales. El usuario revisa las solicitudes antes de aceptar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Export the workout you recommend for me as a single JSON object. Keep using the goals, constraints, preferences, and training history from this conversation. This is for my watch logger; do not change the workout merely to fit the example.\nUse exactly this structure (replace the example values):\n{0}\n{1}\nFor walking, running, mobility or other timed work, use schemaVersion: 2 and an exercise with name and activity: {\"kind\":\"walking\", \"durationSeconds\":900, \"speedKph\":5, \"inclinePercent\":3, \"distanceUnit\":\"km\"}. Duration, distanceMeters, speedKph, inclinePercent and additionalLoad are optional: omit unknown values, never infer actual results from targets. No strength reps or weight fields are needed for timed work. Retain the user's original exercise name and exact variant. Ask about ambiguous modality instead of inventing load. Optional transitionSeconds (0–300) is a separate machine-change timer and never shortens prescribed rest.\nEach strength exercise has one prescribed weight and repetition target for its sets. Split an exercise into separate named entries if its targets vary, such as warm-up and working sets. Weight 0 represents unweighted work; count an assisted machine's displayed load explicitly in its exercise name. Use kg or lb consistently. Weight means the same convention I use in this conversation; clarify per dumbbell versus total in the name. Rest is in seconds. Output JSON only, without commentary.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Export the workout you recommend for me as a single JSON object. Keep using the goals, constraints, preferences, and training history from this conversation. This is for my watch logger; do not change the workout merely to fit the example.\nUse exactly this structure (replace the example values):\n{0}\n{1}\nFor walking, running, mobility or other timed work, use schemaVersion: 2 and an exercise with name and activity: {\"kind\":\"walking\", \"durationSeconds\":900, \"speedKph\":5, \"inclinePercent\":3, \"distanceUnit\":\"km\"}. Duration, distanceMeters, speedKph, inclinePercent and additionalLoad are optional: omit unknown values, never infer actual results from targets. No strength reps or weight fields are needed for timed work. Retain the user's original exercise name and exact variant. Ask about ambiguous modality instead of inventing load. Optional transitionSeconds (0–300) is a separate machine-change timer and never shortens prescribed rest.\nEach strength exercise has one prescribed weight and repetition target for its sets. Split an exercise into separate named entries if its targets vary, such as warm-up and working sets. Weight 0 represents unweighted work; count an assisted machine's displayed load explicitly in its exercise name. Use kg or lb consistently. Weight means the same convention I use in this conversation; clarify per dumbbell versus total in the name. Rest is in seconds. Output JSON only, without commentary."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Exporta el entrenamiento que recomiendas para mí como un único objeto JSON. Conserva los objetivos, restricciones, preferencias e historial de esta conversación. Es para mi registro en el Watch; no cambies el entrenamiento solo para ajustarlo al ejemplo.\nUsa exactamente esta estructura, reemplazando los valores de ejemplo:\n{0}\n{1}\nPara caminar, correr, movilidad u otra actividad por tiempo, usa schemaVersion: 2 y un ejercicio con name y activity: {\"kind\":\"walking\", \"durationSeconds\":900, \"speedKph\":5, \"inclinePercent\":3, \"distanceUnit\":\"km\"}. durationSeconds, distanceMeters, speedKph, inclinePercent y additionalLoad son opcionales: omite datos desconocidos y nunca infieras resultados reales a partir de objetivos. Las actividades por tiempo no necesitan campos de peso o repeticiones de fuerza. Conserva el nombre original y la variante exacta. Pregunta si la modalidad es ambigua en lugar de inventar carga. transitionSeconds (opcional, 0–300) es un tiempo separado para cambiar de máquina; nunca reduce el descanso prescrito.\nCada ejercicio de fuerza tiene un peso y unas repeticiones objetivo para todas sus series. Separa entradas si cambian los objetivos, por ejemplo calentamiento y series de trabajo. weight 0 representa trabajo sin carga; identifica explícitamente la asistencia de una máquina en su nombre. Usa kg o lb de forma consistente. La carga mantiene la convención de esta conversación; aclara por mancuerna o total en el nombre. El descanso va en segundos. Devuelve solo JSON, sin comentarios. Conserva las claves del esquema en inglés."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Enable review notifications in Little Lift → Coach reviews. In Shortcuts, edit Little Lift Review → Automation → Notification; choose Little Lift and filter Title to contain Little Lift. Use Run Immediately only if the OS offers it. The notification is created after the phone saves the completed workout.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Enable review notifications in Little Lift → Coach reviews. In Shortcuts, edit Little Lift Review → Automation → Notification; choose Little Lift and filter Title to contain Little Lift. Use Run Immediately only if the OS offers it. The notification is created after the phone saves the completed workout."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Activa los avisos de revisión en Little Lift → Revisiones del coach. En Atajos, edita Little Lift Review → Automatización → Notificación; elige Little Lift y filtra los títulos que contengan Little Lift. Usa Ejecutar inmediatamente solo si el sistema lo ofrece. El aviso se crea después de guardar el entrenamiento en el teléfono."
          }
        }
      }
    },
